Below is a practical, step‑by‑step playbook you can follow (or adapt) to build a modern, production‑ready front‑end for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole flow – from planning to deployment – and give you concrete code snippets, folder layouts, and tooling choices that work well together.

---

## 1. Planning & Design

| What to do | Why it matters | Tools |
|------------|----------------|-------|
| **Define core features** – product list, detail page, cart, checkout, user account, search, filters, reviews, etc. | Keeps scope focused. | Trello / Notion |
| **Create wireframes** – low‑fidelity sketches of each page. | Visualise layout early. | Figma / Sketch |
| **Build a design system** – colors, typography, spacing, reusable components. | Consistency & faster dev. | Figma components, Storybook |
| **Plan accessibility** – WCAG 2.1 AA, keyboard navigation, ARIA roles. | Legal & inclusive. | axe, Lighthouse |
| **Plan SEO** – semantic HTML, structured data, sitemap, robots.txt. | Organic traffic. | Google Search Console |

---

## 2. Choose a Tech Stack

| Layer | Recommendation | Reason |
|-------|----------------|--------|
| **Framework** | **Next.js** (React) | SSR + SSG + API routes + easy deployment on Vercel |
| **Styling** | **Tailwind CSS** + **Headless UI** | Utility‑first, responsive, no CSS bloat |
| **State** | **Zustand** or **React Context** | Simple, lightweight for cart & auth |
| **Data fetching** | **React Query** | Caching, background refetch, optimistic updates |
| **API** | **REST** (Next.js API routes) or **GraphQL** (Apollo) | Depends on backend; REST is simpler for most e‑commerce |
| **Payments** | **Stripe** (or PayPal SDK) | Secure, PCI‑compliant |
| **Analytics** | **Google Analytics 4** + **Hotjar** | User behavior insights |
| **Testing** | **Jest** + **React Testing Library** | Unit & integration tests |
| **CI/CD** | **GitHub Actions** | Build, lint, test, deploy |
| **Hosting** | **Vercel** (or Netlify) | Zero‑config, instant preview, CDN |

> *If you already have a headless CMS (e.g., Strapi, Sanity) or an e‑commerce API (Shopify, BigCommerce), just swap the data layer.*

---

## 3. Project Skeleton

```
my-ecommerce/
├─ public/
│  ├─ images/
│  └─ favicon.ico
├─ src/
│  ├─ components/
│  │  ├─ ui/          # Headless UI primitives
│  │  ├─ layout/      # Header, Footer, Sidebar
│  │  ├─ product/     # ProductCard, ProductDetail
│  │  └─ cart/        # CartItem, CartSidebar
│  ├─ pages/
│  │  ├─ api/         # Next.js API routes
│  │  ├─ _app.tsx
│  │  ├─ index.tsx    # Home / product listing
│  │  ├─ product/[id].tsx
│  │  ├─ cart.tsx
│  │  ├─ checkout.tsx
│  │  └─ account.tsx
│  ├─ hooks/
│  ├─ lib/
│  │  ├─ api.ts      # Axios instance
│  │  ├─ stripe.ts   # Stripe helper
│  │  └─ auth.ts     # Auth helpers
│  ├─ store/
│  │  └─ cartStore.ts
│  ├─ styles/
│  │  └─ globals.css
│  └─ types/
│     └─ index.d.ts
├─ .env.local
├─ next.config.js
├─ tailwind.config.js
├─ postcss.config.js
├─ jest.config.js
└─ package.json
```

---

## 4. Core Components (Sample Code)

### 4.1 `ProductCard` (React + Tailwind)

```tsx
// src/components/product/ProductCard.tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import Image from 'next/image';

export interface ProductCardProps {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  price: number;
  imageUrl: string;
}

export default function ProductCard({
  id,
  title,
  price,
  imageUrl,
}: ProductCardProps) {
  return (
    <Link href={`/product/${id}`}>
      <a className="block border rounded-lg overflow-hidden hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
        <div className="relative h-48 w-full">
          <Image src={imageUrl} alt={title} layout="fill" objectFit="cover" />
        </div>
        <div className="p-4">
          <h3 className="font-semibold text-sm">{title}</h3>
          <p className="mt-1 text-indigo-600 font-medium">${price.toFixed(2)}</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    </Link>
  );
}
```

### 4.2 `CartSidebar` (Zustand Store + React)

```tsx
// src/store/cartStore.ts
import create from 'zustand';

export interface CartItem {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  price: number;
  quantity: number;
  imageUrl: string;
}

interface CartState {
  items: CartItem[];
  addItem: (item: CartItem) => void;
  removeItem: (id: string) => void;
  clearCart: () => void;
  total: number;
}

export const useCartStore = create<CartState>((set, get) => ({
  items: [],
  addItem: (item) =>
    set((state) => {
      const existing = state.items.find((i) => i.id === item.id);
      if (existing) {
        return {
          items: state.items.map((i) =>
            i.id === item.id ? { ...i, quantity: i.quantity + 1 } : i
          ),
        };
      }
      return { items: [...state.items, { ...item, quantity: 1 }] };
    }),
  removeItem: (id) =>
    set((state) => ({
      items: state.items.filter((i) => i.id !== id),
    })),
  clearCart: () => set({ items: [] }),
  total: () => get().items.reduce((sum, i) => sum + i.price * i.quantity, 0),
}));
```

```tsx
// src/components/cart/CartSidebar.tsx
import { useCartStore } from '../../store/cartStore';
import { XIcon } from '@heroicons/react/solid';

export default function CartSidebar({ isOpen, onClose }: { isOpen: boolean; onClose: () => void }) {
  const items = useCartStore((s) => s.items);
  const total = useCartStore((s) => s.total());

  return (
    <aside
      className={`fixed inset-y-0 right-0 w-80 bg-white shadow-lg transform ${
        isOpen ? 'translate-x-0' : 'translate-x-full'
      } transition-transform duration-300`}
    >
      <div className="flex items-center justify-between p-4 border-b">
        <h2 className="text-lg font-semibold">Your Cart</h2>
        <button onClick={onClose} aria-label="Close cart">
          <XIcon className="h-6 w-6" />
        </button>
      </div>
      <div className="p-4 flex-1 overflow-y-auto">
        {items.length === 0 ? (
          <p className="text-center text-gray-500">Cart is empty.</p>
        ) : (
          items.map((item) => (
            <div key={item.id} className="flex items-center mb-4">
              <Image src={item.imageUrl} alt={item.title} width={50} height={50} />
              <div className="ml-3 flex-1">
                <p className="font-medium">{item.title}</p>
                <p className="text-sm text-gray-600">
                  ${item.price.toFixed(2)} × {item.quantity}
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        )}
      </div>
      <div className="p-4 border-t">
        <div className="flex justify-between font-semibold">
          <span>Total:</span>
          <span>${total.toFixed(2)}</span>
        </div>
        <button
          className="mt-4 w-full bg-indigo-600 text-white py-2 rounded hover:bg-indigo-700"
          onClick={() => {/* navigate to checkout */}}
        >
          Checkout
        </button>
      </div>
    </aside>
  );
}
```

---

## 5. Data Layer

### 5.1 API Wrapper (`src/lib/api.ts`)

```ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
});

export default api;
```

### 5.2 Fetch Products (React Query)

```tsx
// src/hooks/useProducts.ts
import { useQuery } from 'react-query';
import api from '../lib/api';

export interface Product {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  price: number;
  imageUrl: string;
}

export function useProducts() {
  return useQuery<Product[]>('products', async () => {
    const { data } = await api.get('/products');
    return data;
  });
}
```

---

## 6. Checkout Flow

1. **Collect shipping & billing** – use a form library (React Hook Form).
2. **Create a PaymentIntent** – Next.js API route `/api/stripe/create-payment-intent`.
3. **Confirm payment** – Stripe Elements on the client.
4. **Post‑payment** – Save order to DB, send confirmation email.

```ts
// pages/api/stripe/create-payment-intent.ts
import { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from 'next';
import Stripe from 'stripe';

const stripe = new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY!, { apiVersion: '2023-10-16' });

export default async function handler(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  if (req.method !== 'POST') return res.status(405).end();

  const { amount, currency } = req.body;

  try {
    const paymentIntent = await stripe.paymentIntents.create({
      amount,
      currency,
      metadata: { orderId: '12345' },
    });
    res.status(200).json({ clientSecret: paymentIntent.client_secret });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
  }
}
```

---

## 7. Performance & SEO

| Technique | How to implement |
|-----------|------------------|
| **Image optimization** | Use Next.js `<Image>` component; set `priority` on hero images. |
| **Code splitting** | Dynamic imports (`next/dynamic`) for heavy components (e.g., checkout). |
| **Lazy loading** | `loading="lazy"` on `<img>` or use `react-intersection-observer`. |
| **Critical CSS** | Tailwind’s `@apply` + `purge` in production. |
| **Structured data** | Add JSON‑LD in `<Head>` for products (`Product` schema). |
| **Sitemap** | Generate with `next-sitemap` plugin. |
| **Accessibility** | Use semantic tags, `aria-*`, `role`, and test with Lighthouse. |

---

## 8. Testing

```bash
npm install --save-dev jest @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom @testing-library/user-event
```

```js
// jest.config.js
module.exports = {
  testEnvironment: 'jsdom',
  setupFilesAfterEnv: ['<rootDir>/jest.setup.js'],
};
```

```js
// jest.setup.js
import '@testing-library/jest-dom';
```

**Example test**

```tsx
// __tests__/components/ProductCard.test.tsx
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import ProductCard from '../../src/components/product/ProductCard';

test('renders product card with title and price', () => {
  render(
    <ProductCard
      id="1"
      title="Test Product"
      price={19.99}
      imageUrl="/test.jpg"
    />
  );
  expect(screen.getByText(/Test Product/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText(/\$19\.99/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

---

## 9. CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions)

```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml
name: Deploy

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  build-and-deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run build
      - uses: vercel/action@v1
        with:
          vercel-token: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_TOKEN }}
          vercel-org-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_ORG_ID }}
          vercel-project-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID }}
          vercel-args: '--prod'
```

---

## 10. Deployment

1. **Push to GitHub** → GitHub Actions → Vercel deploy.
2. **Set environment variables** in Vercel dashboard (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`, `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, etc.).
3. **Enable CDN** – Vercel automatically serves assets from a global CDN.
4. **Enable HTTPS** – automatic via Vercel.

---

## 11. Post‑Launch Checklist

| Item | Action |
|------|--------|
| **Analytics** | Verify GA4 events (pageview, addToCart, purchase). |
| **Error monitoring** | Set up Sentry for client‑side errors. |
| **Performance** | Run Lighthouse, fix any issues. |
| **SEO audit** | Check indexability, meta tags, structured data. |
| **Accessibility audit** | Run axe, fix violations. |
| **Security** | Ensure HTTPS, CSP headers, secure cookies. |
| **Backup** | Regular database backups. |
| **Monitoring** | UptimeRobot or similar. |

---

## 12. Quick Reference Cheat Sheet

| Topic | Command / Code |
|-------|----------------|
| **Start dev** | `npm run dev` |
| **Build** | `npm run build` |
| **Lint** | `npm run lint` |
